# Mutation cases for "a selector in the caller's environment does not become
# the test's scenario".
#
# Run with `scripts/mutate sce-build/tests/mutations/gate_selectors_do_not_leak.cases`.
#
# The defect was six hand-written subtraction lists. Six test sites drove the
# `mutation-rounds` gate as a subprocess, each clearing the selectors it
# happened to think of; between them they cleared `SCE_MUTATION_ROUNDS` six
# times, `SCE_GATE_CHANGED_FILE` five, the dry-run flag six, and
# `SCE_MUTATION_SHARD` ZERO — while the workflow job that runs those very tests
# sets the shard on purpose. Measured 2026-08-30: with `SCE_MUTATION_SHARD=1/2`
# exported, `the_gate_starts_the_declared_service_for_that_round_and_no_other`
# failed with `names a slice, but 3 casefile(s) are selected`.
#
# The repair replaces the six lists with one DERIVED list and one command
# builder, and these cases attack the three joints that repair rests on: the
# derivation (which name is a selector), the builder (which of them is
# cleared), and the call sites (which shells go through the builder). The
# derivation cases matter more than they look — a scan that reads too little
# reintroduces the leak, and one that reads too much clears a name no caller
# sets, which is the same defect wearing the other sign.
#
# `mutation_rounds_selection.rs` is a RUNTIME target: the oracle reads its text
# rather than linking it, so an edit reaches the verdict without that binary
# being rebuilt. `common/gate_selectors.rs` is a compiled one — it is linked
# into the oracle's own binary.
#
# Anchors are literal slices of the source; an edit that moves one is reported
# INCONCLUSIVE with the anchor quoted, never as a pass.

mutation_tests -p sce-build --test gate_selectors_do_not_leak
mutation_targets sce-build/tests/common/gate_selectors.rs
mutation_runtime_targets sce-build/tests/mutation_rounds_selection.rs

# ── The original defect, restored exactly ──────────────────────────
#
# The set is sorted, so the shard is the name that falls off the end — which
# is the one the six hand-written lists had missed. If only the object check
# noticed this, the probe would be decoration; both must red.

mutation_case "the builder clears all but the last selector" <<'PY'
edit("sce-build/tests/common/gate_selectors.rs",
     """    for name in mutation_rounds_selectors() {
        cmd.env_remove(name);
    }""",
     """    for name in mutation_rounds_selectors().iter().take(3) {
        cmd.env_remove(name);
    }""")
PY

# ── Clearing everything is not clearing the selectors ──────────────
#
# The tempting one-liner. It passes "no selector reached the child" and breaks
# every caller, because a gate started with an empty environment cannot find
# the tools it shells out to.

mutation_case "the builder empties the environment instead" <<'PY'
edit("sce-build/tests/common/gate_selectors.rs",
     """    let mut cmd = Command::new("bash");
    for name in mutation_rounds_selectors() {""",
     """    let mut cmd = Command::new("bash");
    cmd.env_clear();
    for name in mutation_rounds_selectors() {""")
PY

# ── A derivation that reads prose ──────────────────────────────────
#
# A name that survives only in a comment is a name the gate stopped reading.
# Clearing it is a rule kept alive by its own explanation.

mutation_case "the derivation stops stripping comments" <<'PY'
edit("sce-build/tests/common/gate_selectors.rs",
     """        .filter(|line| !line.trim_start().starts_with('#'))
        .collect();""",
     """        .collect();""")
PY

# ── A derivation that cannot tell a local from a selector ──────────

mutation_case "the derivation counts the script's own locals" <<'PY'
edit("sce-build/tests/common/gate_selectors.rs",
     """    if !text.starts_with("SCE_") {
        return None;
    }""",
     """    if text.starts_with("SCE_") {
        return None;
    }""")
PY

# ── A scan that splits a longer identifier ─────────────────────────
#
# Without the name boundary, `MY_SCE_MUTATION_ROUNDS` contributes a selector no
# caller ever sets, and every site clears a ghost.

mutation_case "the scan drops the name boundary" <<'PY'
edit("sce-build/tests/common/gate_selectors.rs",
     "        if starts_a_name && end > i + 4 {",
     "        if starts_a_name || end > i + 4 {")
PY

# ── A call site that goes back to a bare shell ─────────────────────
#
# The seventh site, in the shape it would actually arrive: someone writes a new
# scenario by copying an old one from before this repair.

mutation_case "a call site builds a bare bash again" <<'PY'
edit("sce-build/tests/mutation_rounds_selection.rs",
     """    let out = gate_shell()
        .arg("scripts/gates/mutation-rounds.sh")
        .current_dir(dir.path())""",
     """    let out = Command::new("bash")
        .arg("scripts/gates/mutation-rounds.sh")
        .current_dir(dir.path())""")
PY
